    [BugFix][CI] Keep the image's daily deps in nightly e2e runtime installs (#19104)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    This is a temporary solution; a final method will be provided later.
    
    requirements-nightly.txt, now used by the nightly image layer and the
    e2e runtime install, has no `-r requirements.txt`: that stopped the
    daily torch-npu from being replaced, but it also stopped installing any
    other runtime dependency declared by requirements.txt, so a PR adding
    one would fail with ModuleNotFoundError on a /nightly run.
    
    Install requirements.txt with the packages owned by the image filtered
    out (torch / torch-npu / torchvision / torchaudio, triton-ascend,
    memfabric_hybrid, memcache_hybrid). The daily builds stay untouched
    while every other runtime
    dependency is still installed. `|| true` is required because grep exits
    1 when all lines are filtered out and both run.sh (`set -euo pipefail`)
    and GitHub's bash (`-e -o pipefail`) would abort the step.
    
    Applied to the three single-node nightly workflows and
    tests/e2e/common/multi_node/run.sh.
    
    Tested: yaml.safe_load on the three workflows, `bash -n` on run.sh, and
    the filter run against the real requirements.txt (25 non-comment lines
    kept, none of the seven image-owned packages left); an all-filtered file
    keeps the script
    running and is accepted by pip.
    
    
